WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.900
A private security operations dashboard is a locally controlled workspace for reviewing

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:05.645
security alerts,

00:00:05.645 --> 00:00:08.460
events, assets, video, logs, and system health.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.965
It brings important signals together so an owner or analyst can understand what is

00:00:11.965 --> 00:00:14.980
happening without sending every record to a public service.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:18.835
The dashboard is an operational view, not a complete security product by itself.

00:00:18.835 --> 00:00:22.686
A SIEM collects, searches, correlates, and retains security data at scale.

00:00:22.686 --> 00:00:24.700
An NVR records and retrieves video.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.785
A ticket queue assigns and tracks work.

00:00:26.785 --> 00:00:29.070
The dashboard can surface information from all three,

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:32.000
but it should not pretend to replace their deeper functions.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.310
Useful dashboards connect evidence to decisions.

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:38.260
An alert should lead to relevant context, affected assets, related activity,

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.880
review status, and a clear next action.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.820
Operational indicators should reveal whether cameras, collectors, storage,

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:46.120
and alert channels are healthy enough to trust.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:49.920
Private-first design improves control over sensitive logs, images, credentials,

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.620
and facility information.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:54.065
Local processing can reduce unnecessary disclosure,

00:00:54.065 --> 00:00:56.120
preserve function during an internet outage,

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:59.965
and let the organization define its own retention and access rules.

00:00:59.965 --> 00:01:01.980
Private does not automatically mean secure.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:06.415
The dashboard still needs authentication, patching, segmentation, backups, audit logs,

00:01:06.415 --> 00:01:07.940
and disciplined administration.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:11.345
Local systems can fail or be misconfigured just like hosted systems.

00:01:11.345 --> 00:01:13.900
The practical goal is controlled situational awareness.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:17.825
The dashboard should help authorized people find significant events, review evidence,

00:01:17.825 --> 00:01:18.750
document judgment,

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:22.835
and act responsibly while collecting no more sensitive data than the legitimate security

00:01:22.835 --> 00:01:23.820
purpose requires.
